Severity:
7/10
Problem:
Cant seem to get custom lighting working.
Instances' lighting also dont seem to contribute.
Compiler exits with no issues.
Projected texture lights dont have this problem.
Reproduce:
Open ~/maps/apex/test1.vmf
Compile
No lighting.

Resolution:
New point entities and actual class changes now serialize missing writable FGD defaults.
Compile snapshots also supply missing defaults for existing light entities and copied local
instances, preserving explicit values (including zero) and leaving source maps unchanged.
The reproduction light_rt omitted _light despite the inspector displaying its FGD default.
Native VRAD confirmed its intensity changed from zero to nonzero after this fix.

Instance elevator lights were already contributing, confirmed by native worldlights and the
reporter's follow-up. Mounted PBR addon materials were independently missing from VBSP's
search paths, causing SURF_NOLIGHT/fullbright surfaces. Compilation now uses a temporary
gameinfo with Apex's ordered VFS mounts, without changing the installed game configuration.

Validation:
32 targeted tests (23,540 assertions) and 158 UI tests (4,277 assertions) passed.
Native VBSP, VVIS and VRAD passed on the generated reproduction snapshot, with nonzero custom
light intensity, PBR texinfo flags 0x820 (no SURF_NOLIGHT), and nonzero HDR lightmap samples.
See docs/plans/probe-results/lighting_compilation.md for details.
